{"page": 30, "text": "Consolidated net operating revenues increased by $342 million, or 6.5%, in the three months ended September 30, 2026. The increase of $246 million, or 6.1%, in our Hospital Operations segment\u2019s net operating revenues for the three\u2011month period in 2026 was driven by higher patient volumes as well as continued pricing strength, partially offset by a less favorable payer mix. Additionally, we previously entered into certain agreements with Catholic Health Initiatives (\u201cCHI\u201d), now known as CommonSpirit Health, relating to Conifer, whereby the parties agreed, in part, to the early conclusion and transition of our revenue cycle management services by December 31, 2026 (collectively, the \u201cCHI Agreements\u201d). During the three months ended September 30, 2026, we assessed the periods over which we expect to satisfy the performance obligations under the CHI Agreements based on our current transition progress. We will substantially complete the transition by October 30, 2026 rather than December 31, 2026, as originally expected. As a result, in the three months ended September 30, 2026, we recognized a cumulative catch-up adjustment that increased net operating revenues by $97 million. See Note 1 to the accompanying Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements for additional information regarding the CHI Agreements. 24 Table of Contents Net operating revenues in our Ambulatory Care segment increased by $96 million, or 7.5%, in the three months ended September 30, 2026. This change was primarily driven by our 2025 and 2026 acquisitions, de novo development and purchases of controlling interests, partially offset by the impact of the closure and sale of certain facilities. Same-facility revenue growth, driven by incremental revenue from negotiated commercial rate increases and the addition of new service lines, also contributed to this increase. The following table presents information about selected operating expenses by segment o