{"page": 32, "text": "Salaries, wages and benefits expense for our Hospital Operations segment decreased by $40 million, or 2.1%, in the three months ended September 30, 2026 primarily due to higher employee benefits cost in the 2025 period, partially offset by higher incentive compensation expense in the 2026 period. On a per adjusted admission basis, salaries, wages and benefits expense decreased by 5.7% in the three months ended September 30, 2026. Supplies expense for our Hospital Operations segment increased by $22 million, or 3.7%, during the three months ended September 30, 2026. This change was primarily due to higher patient volumes during the 2026 period, partially offset by our continued focus on cost\u2011efficiency measures. These measures include product standardization, contract management, improved utilization, bulk purchases, focused spending and operational improvements, among others. On a per adjusted admission basis, supplies expense during the three months ended September 30, 2026 was generally consistent with the same period in 2025. Other operating expenses for our Hospital Operations segment increased by $52 million, or 5.6%, in the three months ended September 30, 2026. This change was primarily attributable to increases in malpractice expense and medical fees during the 2026 period. On a per adjusted admission basis, other operating expenses increased by 1.8% in the three months ended September 30, 2026. 25 Table of Contents LIQUIDITY AND CAPITAL RESOURCES OVERVIEW Cash and cash equivalents were $2.674 billion as of September 30, 2026 compared to $2.170 billion as of June 30, 2026. Significant cash flow items in the three months ended September 30, 2026 included: \u2022Net cash provided by operating activities before payments for interest, taxes, restructuring charges, acquisition\u2011related costs, and litigation costs and settlements of $1.562 billion; \u2022Net proceeds from the issuance of an aggregate principal amount of $2.000 billion of our 6.250% senior unsecured notes due September 2034 (the \u201c2034 Senior Notes\u201d); \u2022The redemption, using the issuance proceeds and cash on hand, of all $1.500 billion in aggregate principal amount of our 5.125% senior secured first lien notes due November 2027 (the \u201c2027 Senior Secured First Lien Notes\u201d) and the redemption of $500 million of the then-outstanding $1.750 billion aggregate principal amount of our 6.125% senior unsecured notes due October 2028 (the \u201c2028 Senior Notes\u201d); \u2022Aggregate payments of $255 million to purchase 970 thousand shares of our common stock; \u2022Distributions paid to noncontrolling interests totaling $216 million; \u2022Capital expenditures totaling $198 million; \u2022Income tax payments of $163 million; and \u2022Interest payments of $99 million. Net cash provided by operating activities was $3.507 billion in the nine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to $2.809 billion in the nine months ended September 30, 2025. Key factors contributing to the change between the 2026 and 2025 periods included the\n"}
