nd purchases of controlling interests, partially offset by the impact of the closure and sale of certain facilities, and (2) an increase of $34 million in same\u2011facility salaries, wages and benefits expense. Salaries, wages and benefits expense as a percentage of net operating revenues decreased 40 basis points to 24.3% during the nine months ended September 30, 2026. Supplies Supplies expense increased by $30 million, or 8.9%, during the three months ended September 30, 2026. The change was driven by (1) an $8 million increase related to our 2025 and 2026 acquisitions, de novo development and purchases of controlling interests, partially offset by the impact of the closure and sale of certain facilities, and (2) a $22 million increase in same\u2011facility supplies expense, due primarily to the addition of new service lines. Supplies expense as a percentage of net operating revenues increased to 26.8% for the three months ended September 30, 2026 from 26.4% for the same period in 2025. Supplies expense increased by $106 million,\n"}
